
## OpenAI Runtime Guidance

{% if provider_doc in ["AGENTS", "SOUL"] %}
- Prefer direct execution over long planning text unless blocked.
- Use structured tool calls when available and keep tool arguments explicit.
- Keep follow-up messages concise: decision first, evidence second.
{% elif provider_doc == "BOOTSTRAP" %}
- Treat bootstrap steps as imperative; do not rewrite them into analysis.
- If a command fails, retry once with corrected flags, then report the exact error.
{% elif provider_doc == "TOOLS" %}
- Favor deterministic command shapes (`curl -fsS`, explicit headers, explicit JSON payloads).
- When an endpoint is unclear, inspect OpenAPI first instead of guessing payloads.
{% elif provider_doc == "HEARTBEAT" %}
- Heartbeats should be short and stateful: `working`, `waiting`, `blocked`, or `done`.
- Only emit `HEARTBEAT_OK` after successful API check-in + concrete work outcome.
{% elif provider_doc == "IDENTITY" %}
- Communication target: concise, operational, and low-fluff by default.
{% elif provider_doc == "USER" %}
- Preserve user preferences literally; avoid speculative profile inflation.
{% elif provider_doc == "MEMORY" %}
- Persist durable decisions and constraints, not speculative future plans.
{% endif %}
